            <ArticleTitle>When is a conservative approach best for proximal biceps tendon rupture?</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>134-6</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>This case demonstrates that when a patient's occupation and lifestyle do not require a high degree of supination and upper arm strength, conservative treatment may be the way to go.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
